    "why_ratio_fails_to_separate_forward_lean": "When a user leans forward from the hips toward the laptop screen, their head and shoulders move closer to the camera together. Because perspective projection scales both shoulder width and ear distance by the exact same distance magnification factor (k), the ratio (k * shoulder) / (k * ear) cancels out the distance shift. Consequently, the shoulder-to-ear ratio remains nearly identical (~2.67) between sitting upright and leaning forward.",
